W: 2. The poor little firkin's nine gallons in all
W: Though the beer it is good, the size is too small
W: For lads that are drinkers like you and like I
W: That firkin small barrel too quickly runs dry.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: So bring us a barrel and set it up right
W: Bring us a barrel, to last out the night
W: Bring us a barrel, no matter how high
W: We'll drink it up Lads, we'll drink it dry.
W:
W: 3. And when that I'm dying and on me death bed
W: By me bedside leave a fine full hogshead
W: That if down below I mun go when I die
W: Me and old Nick we will both drink it dry.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. The kilderkin's next and although rather small
W: At least it is better than nothing at all
W: Its eighteen full gallons will just about do
W: Provided, of course, there's another for you.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 5. Then bring forth the Puncheon and roll out the butt
W: Them's the best measures before me to put
W: Our pots will go round and good ale it will flow
W: And we'll be contented for an hour or so.
W: (Chorus:)
%
